diff --git a/doc/ffmpeg.texi b/doc/ffmpeg.texi
index d31678f8d8cd4d4fab586272e0260968f54deb5c..a147bbf843435a041d925574eb85cf714e020c5e 100644
--- a/doc/ffmpeg.texi
+++ b/doc/ffmpeg.texi
@@ -2847,6 +2847,20 @@ to the @option{-ss} option is considered an actual timestamp, and is not
 offset by the start time of the file. This matters only for files which do
 not start from timestamp 0, such as transport streams.
 
+@item -seek_stream @var{stream_specifier} (@emph{input})
+Select the reference stream for the initial input seek requested by
+@option{-ss} or @option{-sseof}. The stream specifier must match exactly one
+stream in this input, for example @code{a:0} for the first audio stream or
+@code{1} for absolute stream index 1. See @ref{Stream specifiers}.
+Invalid specifiers and specifiers matching no streams or multiple streams
+cause an error.
+
+By default, the demuxer selects the reference stream automatically. Selecting
+an output stream with @option{-map} does not select the seek reference.
+This option does not change the timestamp origin, output stream selection,
+or seeks performed by @option{-stream_loop}. Seeking remains subject to the
+demuxer's capabilities and may affect the decodability of other streams.
+
 @item -thread_queue_size @var{size} (@emph{output})
 This option specifies the maximum number of packets per stream that may be
 queued to each muxing thread.
